# This repo is developed on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true`, which rewrites
# checked-out files to CRLF. That is harmless for source Git never hands to a
# shell — but fatal for anything a Linux container executes or parses.
#
# `scripts/*.sh` are bind-mounted into the `backup` container and run there. A
# CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for an interpreter literally named
# "/bin/sh\r", and the container dies with an unhelpful "no such file or
# directory" naming a path that plainly exists. Same class of problem for the
# Dockerfile and Caddyfile, which are parsed inside Linux images.
#
# Forcing LF on checkout for these paths costs nothing on Windows — no editor
# in use here needs CRLF — and removes the failure entirely.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
Caddyfile text eol=lf
docker-compose*.yml text eol=lf
.env.production.example text eol=lf

# Generated bundles; never diffed by hand.
dist/** -diff
